  "presentation_summary": [
    "26-year-old man was found unresponsive in a car while working manual labor outdoors at 31 C.",
    "On admission he had GCS 3, HR 131/min, RR 28/min, BP 128/63 mmHg, oxygen saturation 95%, and core body temperature 42.2 C.",
    "Initial labs included potassium 5.4 mmol/L, bicarbonate 17 mmol/L, urea 23 mmol/L, creatinine 204 umol/L, CK 984 U/L, INR 1.3, platelet count 157 x10^9/L, and mixed metabolic/respiratory acidosis.",
    "Within 24 hours he developed oliguria, DIC, severe liver failure, platelets 26 x10^9/L, INR 8.3, fibrinogen 75 mg/dL, AST 9129 U/L, and ALT 6679 U/L.",
    "He underwent plasma exchange and urgent liver transplantation on day 2 after admission, with eventual good recovery."
  ],
